2) “Vital Areas” engineering placement (where each goes)

1) Dwelling Sector (Residential)

Place on ring for stable artificial-G.
   •   Quiet side away from heavy industry and docking vibration paths
   •   Radiation storm shelters embedded near structural ribs
   •   Air quality zoning: kitchens/garbage chutes separated from living air loop

2) Hospital / Medical Center

Split design (recommended):
   •   Ring medical wing (main): surgery + wards under artificial-G (better for most care)
   •   Core micro-G wing (specialty): rehabilitation research, fluid shift studies, certain procedures
Hard requirements:
   •   Dedicated clean power, redundant O₂, sterilization loops
   •   Isolation rooms + biohazard handling + med gas storage

3) Marketplace / Food / Retail

Ring, near transit nodes (high foot traffic).
   •   Food cold chain tied into thermal management (waste heat reuse)
   •   Smart inventory using autonomous carts + RFID/vision (low labor load)

4) Office Center / Governance

Ring or near spoke bases (best compromise):
   •   Close to population but buffered from market noise
   •   Direct redundant links to core mission ops (data center)

5) Research Labs

Two-tier lab model:
   •   Ring labs: biology, materials under partial-G, manufacturing lines
   •   Core labs: micro-G experiments, crystal growth, advanced assembly
Safety: labs in compartmentalized pressure pods with fast isolation doors.

6) Library / Learning Center

Ring, central & calm (community stability).
   •   Also acts as civil shelter (thick shielding zone)
   •   Education nodes connected to simulation/VR from core compute

7) Agriculture & Life Support Zone

Ring outer belt (as you already did) is smart:
   •   Crops benefit from gravity for soil/water handling
   •   Close to water processing and CO₂ scrubbing farms
   •   Waste → bio-reactor → fertilizer → crops loop

8) Recreation & Green Zones

Ring, distributed to reduce crowd pressure.
   •   Serve as psychological health infrastructure
   •   Multi-use: sports + parks + emergency assembly points

